\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {8.1}{\ignorespaces In the black hole mirror model, the event horizon acts as a $CPT$-symmetric mirror connecting the exterior of our universe to the exterior of anti-universe. Infalling matter from our universe annihilates with infalling antimatter from the anti-universe at the horizon. The KD-Majorana condition provides a fundamental explanation for why the universe and anti-universe must remain perfectly $CPT$-symmetric, even at quantum scales.}}{108}{figure.caption.38}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:annihilate_BHmirror}{{8.1}{108}{In the black hole mirror model, the event horizon acts as a $CPT$-symmetric mirror connecting the exterior of our universe to the exterior of anti-universe. Infalling matter from our universe annihilates with infalling antimatter from the anti-universe at the horizon. The KD-Majorana condition provides a fundamental explanation for why the universe and anti-universe must remain perfectly $CPT$-symmetric, even at quantum scales}{figure.caption.38}{}}
\newlabel{fig:annihilate_BHmirror@cref}{{[figure][1][8]8.1}{[1][107][]108}}
